 ## Overview
-This method transfers intersection computation from geometric space to image space by rasterizing model surfaces into 2D textures, enabling collision detection and volumetric rendering at real-time frame rates [S1, unofficial]. It differs from slicing-based voxelization by rasterizing the model approximately once rather than $N$ times (where $N$ is the volume resolution along $z$), making performance insensitive to scene complexity [S1, unofficial]. Unlike Layered Depth Image (LDI) extraction, it is view-independent and avoids CPU-side sorting of depth lists [S1, unofficial]. Builds on [Position Map and Image-Space Transfer](6237-position-map-and-image-space-transfer.md). Siblings: [Position Map Voxelization](2604-position-map-voxelization.md), [Billboard Voxelization](2659-billboard-voxelization.md).
+This method transfers intersection computation from geometric space to image space by rasterizing model surfaces into 2D textures, enabling collision detection and volumetric rendering at real-time frame rates [S1, unofficial]. It differs from slicing-based voxelization by rasterizing the model approximately once rather than $N$ times (where $N$ is the volume resolution along $z$), making performance insensitive to scene complexity [S1, unofficial]. Unlike Layered Depth Image (LDI) extraction, it is view-independent and avoids CPU-side sorting of depth lists [S1, unofficial]. Builds on [Position Map and Image-Space Transfer](6237-position-map-and-image-space-transfer.md) [G]. Siblings: [Position Map Voxelization](2604-position-map-voxelization.md), [Billboard Voxelization](2659-billboard-voxelization.md) [G].
 
